  "body": "While I was investigating why Synapse 0.99 appeared to be slower than Synapse 0.34 (#4713), I tried disabling the .well-known lookup in the federation agent. Doing so appeared to make my synapse settle at 1.5G of memory usage rather than 2G.\r\n\r\n> The .well-known cache sits at around 1500 entries, so I can't believe it's all coming from there - it would imply about 333K per entry, which seems immense. I wonder if the connection pool is hanging on to data it shouldn't. It would probably be fruitful to investigate with a memory profiler.",
